18612	18756	18610	18610	Helen	481	“ is huge Ajax , bulwark of the Achaeans , and on the other side of him , among the Cretans , stands Idomeneus looking like a god , and with the captains of the Cretans round him . Often did Menelaus receive him as a guest in our house when he came visiting us from Crete . I see , moreover , many other Achaeans whose names I could tell you , but there are two whom I can nowhere find , Castor , breaker of horses , and Pollux the mighty boxer ; they are children of my mother , and own brothers to myself . Either they have not left Lacedaemon , or else , though they have brought their ships , they will not show themselves in battle for the shame and disgrace that I have brought upon them . ”
