65969	66063	65960	65960	Dolon	809	“ Hector , with his vain flattering promises , lured me from my better judgement . He said he would give me the horses of the noble son of Peleus and his bronze - bedizened chariot ; he bade me go through the darkness of the flying night , get close to the enemy , and find out whether the ships are still guarded as heretofore , or whether , now that we have beaten them , the Achaeans design to fly , and through sheer exhaustion are neglecting to keep their watches . ”
