70350	70449	70347	70347	she	448	“ Hector son of Priam , peer of gods in counsel , father Jove has sent me to bear you this message — so long as you see Agamemnon heading his men and making havoc of the Trojan ranks , you are to keep aloof and bid the others bear the brunt of the battle , but when Agamemnon is wounded either by spear or arrow , and takes to his chariot , then will Jove vouchsafe you strength to slay till you reach the ships , and till night falls at the going down of the sun . ”
